# %% [markdown]
# NEXUS Alpha v3: Can chart images, SEC filing text, or both predict where a stock goes next?

**A leakage-controlled comparison of 7 computer-vision models and 6 language models (plus baselines) on 50 US stocks in 5 sectors, 2016-10 to 2026-10, at 5, 10, 20 and 40 trading-day horizons.**

Master of Applied Artificial Intelligence, University of Wollongong in Dubai. Final project (Computer Vision + Natural Language Processing).

> Educational research. Not financial advice. A predictive association is not a cause.

**This notebook is the only entry point.** It downloads nothing it cannot verify, trains every model, picks winners on validation data only, freezes those choices, scores the locked test period once, writes a Streamlit dashboard and generates three PDF reports (Computer Vision, NLP, and Multimodal). Every number in the reports is read from files this run saved; no number is typed in by hand.

| Item | Setting |
|---|---|
| Stocks | 50 (10 per sector: Information Technology, Financials, Health Care, Consumer Discretionary, Communication Services) |
| Prices | Verified 1-week, 1-day and 1-hour bars (TriFrame tier-A store, every file SHA-256 checked), plus SPY |
| Text | SEC EDGAR 10-K, 10-Q and 8-K filings of the same 50 companies, downloaded in this notebook with point-in-time acceptance timestamps |
| Decisions | 2016-10-10 to 2026-08 (10 years of decision dates; older bars are used only to draw the first charts) |
| Targets | (a) direction: DOWN / SIDEWAYS / UP, (b) realised volatility, (c) a drawdown of more than 10% — each over 5, 10, 20 and 40 sessions |
| Blocks | train 2016-10 → 2020-12 · inner 2021 (early stopping, calibration) · validation 2022-2023 (all model selection) · **test 2024-01 → 2026-08 (locked, opened once after the freeze)** |
| CV models | Custom CNN (Jiang-Kelly-Xiu style, from scratch), ResNet-50, EfficientNet-B0, ConvNeXt-Tiny, ViT-B/16, Swin-T, YOLOv8 (classification backbone; plus the ready-made YOLOv8 chart-pattern detector as a zero-shot extra) |
| NLP models | TF-IDF + logistic/ridge (baseline), FinBERT, SEC-BERT, RoBERTa-large, Longformer-4096, DeBERTa-v3-large, FinGPT (Llama-2-7B + FinGPT LoRA) |

# %% [markdown]
## 0. Feasibility check of the original plan (read before running)

**Verdict: the project can be done, with six changes.** Each change is forced by data or by how a model works, not by results (no result existed when they were made).

| # | Original plan | What this notebook does | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 50 named stocks | **44 kept, 6 replaced within the same sector**: AVGO→TXN, CRM→ADBE (IT); BKNG→MAR (Consumer Discretionary); CMCSA→META, TMUS→OMC, EA→NYT (Communication Services). GOOGL is represented by **GOOG** (same company, Alphabet class C; prices nearly identical) | The six have no verified 10-year **hourly** bars in our store (Yahoo gives only 730 days of hourly data). Replacing them keeps 10 stocks per sector. 16 same-sector reserves are in the data package; section 3 swaps one in automatically, by a rule fixed in advance, if a stock fails the SEC check |
| 2 | "Candlestick movement" | Interpreted as the **3-class direction** of the price (DOWN / SIDEWAYS / UP) over each horizon, with a volatility-scaled sideways band | A class must be defined before it can be predicted; a fixed band (e.g. ±1%) would make "sideways" mean different things for a utility-like and a volatile stock |
| 3 | YOLOv8 "detects candlestick patterns; ready-made weights" | Two uses: **(a)** YOLOv8s-cls ImageNet backbone fine-tuned on our task exactly like the other six (this is the model in every comparison); **(b)** the public detector `foduucom/stockmarket-pattern-detection-yolov8` (6 chart patterns, published mAP@0.5 ≈ 0.61) used zero-shot as pattern features | A detector outputs boxes, not up/down/volatility. Using its detections as features is the honest way to test "ready-made chart-pattern weights" |
| 4 | "RoBERTa-large (Financial)" | `FacebookAI/roberta-large` (general), fine-tuned on our filings | No established financial RoBERTa-large checkpoint exists; fine-tuning on SEC text is what makes it financial |
| 5 | FinGPT "LoRA fine-tuned" | FinGPT's published LoRA (`FinGPT/fingpt-mt_llama2-7b_lora`) on Llama-2-7B, loaded in 4-bit, used as a **frozen** encoder (embeddings + its native sentiment read-out). Optional QLoRA switch (off) | 7B parameters: a full fine-tune for 12 targets does not fit the budget. Llama-2 is gated (Meta licence accepted on the `HF_TOKEN` account). If loading fails, FinGPT is reported as Not Run and the study has 5 language models |
| 6 | 10 years, 1W/1D/1H charts | Decision dates 2016-10-10 → 2026-08 (labels need 40 sessions after the last decision; data end 2026-10-09). Charts: 52 weekly, 63 daily, 70 hourly candles | Exactly the requested span. The **test period (2024-2026) begins after the pre-training cut-off of every language model used** (Llama-2's data end 2022; DeBERTa-v3 2021; others earlier), so no text model can "remember" test-period news |

**What will probably happen (stated before any result, so the reports cannot be accused of hindsight).** Earlier projects on the same data (TriFrame, NEXUS V1, the SEC filings study) found: volatility is predictable (persistence), drawdown risk is partly predictable, **direction is close to chance**, and chart images or filing text add little once simple numbers are known. This study is designed so that a null result is still a clear, defensible finding.

**Run it in this order.** (1) Upload `nav3_bars_66.zip` to `MyDrive/antigravity_workspace/nexus_alpha_v3/data/`. (2) Colab Secrets: `HF_TOKEN` and `SEC_USER_AGENT` ("Your Name your.email@domain"), *Notebook access* ON. (3) Accept the Llama-2 licence (only needed for FinGPT). (4) Runtime → A100 GPU, High-RAM. (5) Run all with `RUN_MODE = "QUICK_VERIFY"` (about 1-1.5 h, 10 stocks, short training: a pipeline check, stamped "not research results"). (6) Switch to `"FULL_RESEARCH"` and Run all (about 8-10 h the first time; the SEC download is cached). Every stage saves to Drive and resumes after a disconnect.

