## 0.1 Where each project question is answered

| Question (from the project brief) | Development answer (validation) | Final answer (locked test) |
|---|---|---|
| Q1. Can CV, NLP, or CV+NLP predict UP/SIDEWAYS/DOWN at 5/10/20/40 days? | §20 | §23.1 |
| Q2. Which CV model is best over the 50 stocks, and why? | §12.1 | §23.2 |
| Q3. Which CV model combination is best (e.g. CNN+ResNet, EfficientNet+ResNet…)? | §12.2 | §23.3 |
| Q4. Which model or combination best predicts (a) direction, (b) volatility, (c) a >10% drawdown? | §12.1-12.2 | §23.3 |
| Q5. Which model works best in which sector; is any network sector-specific? | §12.3 | §23.4 |
| Q6. Which report moves the market more: 10-K, 10-Q or 8-K? | §14 (event study), §18 | §23.5 |
| Q7. In which sectors do filings move prices more? | §14, §18 | §23.5 |
| Q8. What in the reports moves the market? | §15 (words), §18.3 (8-K items, tone, attributions) | §23.5 |
| Q9. Which sectors are sensitive to which report type? | §14 (sector × form) | §23.5 |
| Q10. Does combining the top-3 CV and top-3 NLP models add predictive edge? | §20 | §23.1 |
| Stronger baselines, do CV/NLP add to simple numbers? (post-hoc, after the test was opened) | | §23A |
| Combinations of networks (within and across modalities), interpretable text features, hypothesis register, v3.1 protocol (post-hoc) | | §23B |
| Product: Streamlit dashboard (4 stocks × 1W/1D/1H screenshots + filing summary → UP/SIDEWAYS/DOWN + 20-day Monte Carlo) | §21 (simulator check) | §24 |
| Three reports: CV, NLP, Multimodal | | §25 |

